From: cl2t <yihong.or@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: expect JSON after nats-server removed JSONP

In nats-server 2.15.1, server.ResponseHandler ignores JSONP callback
query parameters and always sets Content-Type to application/json.
Update the monitoring callback test expectation to match; production
code is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [upstream repository archived]
Reference: https://github.com/nats-io/nats-server/blob/v2.15.1/server/monitor.go

Signed-off-by: cl2t <yihong.or@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
diff --git a/server/monitor_test.go b/server/monitor_test.go
index be9fda5..55cb88a 100644
--- a/server/monitor_test.go
+++ b/server/monitor_test.go
@@ -43,7 +43,6 @@ const (
 	monitorPort  = 8222
 	expectedJSON = "application/json"
 	expectedText = "text/html; charset=utf-8"
-	expectedCb   = "application/javascript"
 )
 
 var defaultMonitorOptions = natsd.Options{
@@ -315,8 +314,8 @@ func TestMonitorServerz(t *testing.T) {
 	}
 	resp.Body.Close()
 
-	// Test JSONP
-	resp, _ = getBody(t, ServerPath+"?callback=callback", expectedCb)
+	// Current nats-server ResponseHandler ignores JSONP callbacks and returns JSON.
+	resp, _ = getBody(t, ServerPath+"?callback=callback", expectedJSON)
 	resp.Body.Close()
 
 	// Restart server, for memory based server, things should have been reset
